{
  "an5.58:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 5.58 ",
  "an5.58:0.2": "6. Hindrances ",
  "an5.58:0.3": "The Licchavi Youths ",
  "an5.58:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Vesālī, at the Great Wood, in the hall with the peaked roof. ",
  "an5.58:1.2": "Then the Buddha robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Vesālī for alms. ",
  "an5.58:1.3": "Then after the meal, on his return from almsround, he plunged deep into the Great Wood and sat at the root of a tree for the day’s meditation. ",
  "an5.58:2.1": "Now at that time several Licchavi youths took strung bows and, escorted by a pack of hounds, were going for a walk in the Great Wood when they saw the Buddha seated at the root of a tree. ",
  "an5.58:2.2": "When they saw him, they put down their strung bows, dispatched their hounds to one side, and went up to him. They bowed and silently paid homage to the Buddha with cupped palms. ",
  "an5.58:3.1": "Now at that time Mahānāma the Licchavi was going for a walk in the Great Wood when he saw those Licchavi youths silently paying homage to the Buddha with cupped palms. ",
  "an5.58:3.2": "Seeing this, he went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, ",
  "an5.58:3.3": "and expressed this heartfelt sentiment, ",
  "an5.58:3.4": "“They will become Vajjis! They will become Vajjis!” ",
  "an5.58:4.1": "“But Mahānāma, why do you say that ",
  "an5.58:4.2": "they will become Vajjis?” ",
  "an5.58:4.3": "“Sir, these Licchavi youths are violent, harsh, and brash. ",
 